# lightweight-rec configuration.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/record/config and uncomment what you need. skhd does not
# load your shell rc, so Option+R sees this file and nothing else.
#
# Plain shell assignments, one per line: `record` sources this file, so a syntax
# error here breaks the hotkey. Every key below is optional and shows its
# default. The same list, with the detail, is the Configuration table in the
# README.
#
# Only RECORD_DIR is destructive: every start deletes this tool's own mp4 files
# older than RECORD_DAYS at its top level, so give it a directory of its own.
# The install-time flag (--with-handy) goes on the ./install.sh command line,
# never in here.

# Where the mp4 files, the logs and the whisper model live.
# RECORD_DIR="$HOME/Recordings"

# Root of your Obsidian vault: the folder that has a .obsidian directory in it.
# RECORD_VAULT="$HOME/Documents/Obsidian"

# Folder the note is filed in. Outside a vault, the stop warns you and says where.
# RECORD_NOTES="$RECORD_VAULT/Recordings"

# Display to capture, as an ffmpeg avfoundation index. List them: record screens
# RECORD_SCREEN=0

# Microphone by device name, exactly as ffmpeg lists it; empty resolves one on
# every start. Check what a start would open with: record mic
# RECORD_MIC=""

# 1 mixes in what the Mac plays, the other side of a call included, captured
# natively (no driver, output device untouched). 0 records the microphone
# alone, so on headphones only your own voice.
# RECORD_SYSTEM_AUDIO=1

# What writes the title, tags, summary and screen description. Either a CLI
# you already have installed and signed in (install.sh does not touch it):
#
#   claude      cursor      copilot
#
# or a model server spoken to over HTTP, in the protocol they all share:
#
#   ollama      on this Mac, http://localhost:11434/v1, no key
#   lmstudio    on this Mac, http://localhost:1234/v1, no key
#   openai      OPENAI_API_KEY
#   anthropic   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   gemini      GEMINI_API_KEY
#   openrouter  OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   custom      anything else that speaks it: set RECORD_AI_URL
#
# ollama and lmstudio are the only settings in which the screen frames and the
# transcript stay on this Mac and the note is still complete. 0 makes no call
# at all: no egress, and no title, tags, summary or screen text either.
# RECORD_AI=claude

# The model each call uses, in the id the backend itself lists. Empty picks a
# default: claude sonnet then haiku, cursor cursor-grok-4.6-high, copilot and
# gemini gemini-3.8-flash, openai gpt-5.4-mini, anthropic claude-sonnet-5 then
# claude-haiku-4-5, openrouter google/gemini-3.8-flash. For ollama and
# lmstudio, empty means the first model the server lists, which is what you
# want with one model installed and not what you want with five. Screen frames
# first, then title and summary.
# RECORD_AI_VISION_MODEL=""
# RECORD_AI_META_MODEL=""

# The endpoint, when it is not the default of the backend named above: another
# Mac on the network, a gateway, a server on a port of its own. It must be the
# base that has /chat/completions under it, so end it at /v1. Required by
# RECORD_AI=custom, optional for everything else.
# RECORD_AI_URL=""

# The API key, when the provider's usual variable is not set or you would
# rather keep it here. It never reaches the command line: curl reads it from a
# file this script writes 600 in its scratch directory and deletes on the way
# out. Local servers need none.
# RECORD_AI_KEY=""

# How many of the frames extracted from one video a single HTTP screen call
# carries, evenly spread over the hour. A chat request holds every image it
# names, so this is what keeps a local model on a laptop from being handed
# thirty at once. The CLIs ignore it: they read the frames off disk themselves.
# RECORD_AI_FRAMES=8

# Seconds one HTTP call may take before curl gives up. A small model on a Mac
# reading eight frames is slower than an API, so this is generous.
# RECORD_AI_TIMEOUT=600

# The old name of the off switch. 0 still means no call at all.
# RECORD_CLAUDE=1

# Retention in days for this tool's own mp4 files in RECORD_DIR.
# RECORD_DAYS=14

# App to open once the capture is up, by its name. Empty opens nothing.
# RECORD_LAUNCH_APP=""

# The red dot overlay, if you moved it out of ~/bin.
# RECORD_DOT="$HOME/bin/record-dot"

# The system audio helper, if you moved it out of ~/bin.
# RECORD_AUDIO="$HOME/bin/record-audio"

# The config file itself: read from the environment, so setting it here does nothing.
# RECORD_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/record/config"
